WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.270
Now running in <i>Monthly Midnight!</i>

00:00.000 --> 00:02.270
10 volumes now on sale!

00:00.000 --> 00:02.270
TV anime broadcast begins next spring!

00:00.000 --> 00:02.270
Finally over 10 million copies sold!

00:06.440 --> 00:07.690
Nice!

00:08.570 --> 00:10.010
Is it emotional enough?!

00:10.230 --> 00:12.040
It is, it is!

00:13.860 --> 00:17.600
Until now, you've tended to skirt around
 scenes like this out of embarrassment.

00:17.600 --> 00:20.790
But you nailed this one, 
and it's <i>really</i> good.

00:21.300 --> 00:24.040
It's a relief to hear you say that.

00:24.230 --> 00:25.900
You're in the zone.

00:25.900 --> 00:27.530
Did something good happen?

00:29.540 --> 00:30.740
Just kidding!

00:33.550 --> 00:36.050
<b>Hiiragi Apartments</b>

00:34.400 --> 00:35.690
I'm home.

00:39.190 --> 00:41.060
That went great!

00:42.650 --> 00:44.620
He approved the rough draft.

00:51.440 --> 00:55.930
<i>It's thanks to Goshiki-san. 
Or, maybe it's rude to say so.</i>

00:56.620 --> 01:00.040
<i>But I'd like to see that 
look on her face again.</i>

01:00.040 --> 01:03.230
<i>Maybe I'll spend some time with 
her before I start drawing.</i>

01:05.660 --> 01:07.070
Goshiki-san.

01:07.470 --> 01:08.570
Kuga-san.

01:09.390 --> 01:11.720
Um, I'm done with the rough draft.

01:11.720 --> 01:13.720
Oh, that's good to hear.

01:14.190 --> 01:15.520
And so...

01:19.160 --> 01:22.720
I-I'd like to ask you to 
do the next batch of work.

01:23.540 --> 01:24.730
Work time!

01:24.730 --> 01:27.810
Yeah, it won't be long from now.

01:28.710 --> 01:31.470
<i>I ended up talking about work.</i>

01:31.900 --> 01:33.470
Thank you—

01:36.130 --> 01:37.180
What's the matter?

03:09.960 --> 03:14.960
<b><b>Episode 6</b></b>

03:09.960 --> 03:14.960
<b><b>A Letter</b></b>

03:09.960 --> 03:14.960
<b><b>with the Princess</b></b>

03:16.010 --> 03:17.710
Did something happen?

03:18.620 --> 03:24.080
The other day, I stopped by two 
places to try out as an assistant.

03:24.080 --> 03:26.590
Right, you did mention that.

03:27.180 --> 03:32.350
And earlier, I received this 
email from the first artist.

03:30.600 --> 03:34.610
To Shiori Goshiki-sama

03:30.600 --> 03:34.610
It was very helpful that
you were so diligent as
an assistant by
complying with my
sudden request for help.

03:30.600 --> 03:34.610
I apologize, but I think
having you continue
here would be difficult
due to design-related
discrepancies.
However, I do think
you could do work
for other artists.

03:34.840 --> 03:37.600
D-Design-related discrepancies, huh?

03:38.410 --> 03:43.610
I did think my pen technique was weak, and that
 I wouldn't have contributed much right away.

03:46.740 --> 03:50.200
But there aren't many local 
artists who haven't gone digital,

03:50.200 --> 03:53.420
and I would have welcomed the 
chance to get regular work.

03:53.420 --> 03:57.560
This happens a lot. 
There's no need to worry about it so much.

03:57.560 --> 03:58.870
What about the other place?

03:59.430 --> 04:02.660
I haven't heard back yet.

04:02.660 --> 04:05.860
Honestly, I suspect it'll be hard 
to become a regular there, too.

04:05.860 --> 04:07.900
Wh-Why?

04:07.900 --> 04:11.890
There's the technical aspect,
 and it may be the case that...

04:12.710 --> 04:14.030
It's nice to meet you.

04:14.700 --> 04:18.660
I am Shiori Goshiki, 
and I hope to be your assistant.

04:18.660 --> 04:21.130
Here's hoping things go well today.

04:22.310 --> 04:23.940
<i>An upper-class lady persona?</i>

04:24.610 --> 04:26.650
I'm Sano. Nice to meet you.

04:28.160 --> 04:33.330
It's a digital/analog hybrid, and I'd 
have you draw backgrounds by hand.

04:33.330 --> 04:35.670
Then someone else would 
do the finishing touches.

04:36.260 --> 04:37.780
Just leave it to me!

04:38.290 --> 04:41.430
I've already practiced 
plenty with your work.

04:41.430 --> 04:43.660
Oh... cool.

04:43.920 --> 04:50.160
<i>I wasn't able to fully help out at that last 
assistant gig, so I've got to try hard today!</i>

04:51.680 --> 04:53.050
I'm done!

04:53.050 --> 04:56.430
Hey, good work. The small 
bits are drawn well, too.

04:57.380 --> 04:59.060
Thank you!

04:59.060 --> 05:00.600
I studied up.

05:00.600 --> 05:03.200
Ah, you actually have read it!

05:03.450 --> 05:06.020
Yes, it was very interesting.

05:06.020 --> 05:07.450
I've become a fan.

05:07.720 --> 05:08.690
For real?!

05:08.690 --> 05:09.590
Yes.

05:09.590 --> 05:14.460
E-Even though there are heaps of 
magical girl stories out there.

05:15.650 --> 05:17.200
Heaps?

05:17.740 --> 05:22.630
You know, like the definitive classic 
<i>Magical Girl-Thing From Another World</i>,

05:22.630 --> 05:26.260
or the recent <i>Mystic Knight Cappuccino</i>.

05:26.760 --> 05:29.400
Sorry, I'm under-informed.

05:29.830 --> 05:34.470
It's only been about a year since 
I've started reading or drawing manga.

05:35.480 --> 05:37.560
Oh, okay.

05:37.560 --> 05:39.670
<i>You're still new to it?</i>

05:40.160 --> 05:42.850
Was your family strict?

05:42.850 --> 05:45.620
Oh, are you a <i>real</i> upper-class lady?

05:46.150 --> 05:47.260
A real...

05:47.730 --> 05:50.110
No, in my family, I'm a princess.

05:53.620 --> 05:54.630
A princess?

05:55.770 --> 05:58.860
<i>Maybe I should keep the 
princess thing secret.</i>

05:59.170 --> 06:01.120
That is, it's a hobby.

06:01.460 --> 06:03.130
A-A hobby.

06:03.360 --> 06:05.430
Yes, a hobby.

06:05.820 --> 06:09.850
I go around... acting like... a princess.

06:10.780 --> 06:12.820
I-Is that so?

06:18.070 --> 06:20.260
<i>I ended up deceiving him.</i>

06:21.600 --> 06:24.410
"Princess" is an unusual hobby.

06:24.410 --> 06:27.020
Oh, but I don't mean that in a bad way.

06:28.600 --> 06:31.790
It seems really out there, but that's cool.

06:34.860 --> 06:35.850
Never mind.

06:40.970 --> 06:44.610
After that, the mood was a little, well...

06:44.610 --> 06:47.910
Maybe we had a failure to communicate.

06:48.230 --> 06:51.100
You consider that a failure?

06:51.100 --> 06:52.930
Sometimes it's a good fit, sometimes not.

06:53.240 --> 06:59.550
Yes, but even so, I suspect 
the cause lies with me.

07:00.380 --> 07:04.320
Aren't you getting that tablet 
from Moka-nee next Sunday?

07:04.320 --> 07:08.560
If you learn the ropes, I'm sure you 
could soon become a digital assistant.

07:08.890 --> 07:11.570
I'm sure there'll be other 
workplaces that are good fits!

07:13.160 --> 07:15.110
Thank you.

07:16.890 --> 07:20.760
<i>I want to encourage her, 
but it's about work.</i>

07:20.760 --> 07:23.090
<i>I shouldn't get too involved.</i>

07:24.230 --> 07:28.250
Um, Goshiki-san, didn't you write 
a list of things you want to do?

07:28.250 --> 07:29.080
Yes.

07:29.330 --> 07:32.470
I wonder if there's anything 
I can help you with.

07:33.680 --> 07:37.340
I-I want you to cheer up!

07:44.700 --> 07:47.210
Wouldn't some meat cheer her up?

07:47.210 --> 07:48.220
Wouldn't it?

07:48.540 --> 07:49.630
Meat?

07:49.630 --> 07:51.260
Wait, you were listening?!

07:51.260 --> 07:53.370
Is that a "no," then?

07:53.370 --> 07:56.960
You know, I did say we'd go 
once I was done with work,

07:56.960 --> 07:59.250
but one thing or another kept us from it.

07:59.250 --> 08:02.590
But that's not one of the things 
Goshiki-san wants to do.

08:02.590 --> 08:04.170
We can go some other time.

08:04.170 --> 08:05.010
No.

08:05.380 --> 08:08.950
There's an item on my list 
that says "celebratory meat."

08:09.770 --> 08:13.700
These things you want to do 
aren't such high hurdles.

08:14.480 --> 08:15.520
Well, then...

08:15.970 --> 08:17.070
Let's go!

08:18.430 --> 08:20.800
Yay! Barbecue!

08:20.800 --> 08:22.390
'Becue!

08:23.340 --> 08:25.570
The barbecue place where we're going...

08:25.570 --> 08:28.520
has good meat, and good curry, too!

08:28.520 --> 08:29.480
Curry?

08:30.240 --> 08:33.190
It has tons of 
melt-in-your-mouth meat in it!

08:33.580 --> 08:35.560
Fumio loves it, too!

08:35.560 --> 08:36.640
Love it.

08:36.900 --> 08:40.770
It's unusual for a barbecue place 
to be known for its curry.

08:40.770 --> 08:42.290
I can't wait.

08:42.290 --> 08:43.670
Oh, we're here!

08:45.040 --> 08:47.540
<b>Barbecue Restaurant It's Beef!</b>

08:45.530 --> 08:47.170
It's Beef!

08:48.160 --> 08:49.310
Oh, my!

08:50.580 --> 08:53.300
So this is yakiniku barbecue!

08:54.130 --> 08:56.550
Is this your first time trying it?

08:56.790 --> 09:00.980
I've participated in barbecues with 
the children's group on the island.

09:00.980 --> 09:05.050
We have a yakiniku restaurant, 
but I've never been to it.

09:07.100 --> 09:08.160
Lovely!

09:08.860 --> 09:10.550
I'm glad for you.

09:11.290 --> 09:17.580
According to things I've read, manga 
artists eat meat and live with animals.

09:17.580 --> 09:19.800
That's a rather skewed perspective.

09:19.800 --> 09:23.730
Sorry, our place doesn't allow pets.

09:25.810 --> 09:27.030
That's true.

09:27.030 --> 09:30.460
But I'm happy with just the meat.

09:31.500 --> 09:33.580
Let's go ahead and flip the meat.

09:34.680 --> 09:35.710
Don't touch it with those!

09:37.030 --> 09:38.790
Use the tongs.

09:38.790 --> 09:40.950
Those long chopsticks are for salad!

09:41.520 --> 09:45.360
All right. Wh-What about this onion on top?

09:45.360 --> 09:48.240
Leave it on top, and just grill one side!

09:48.550 --> 09:52.330
That makes sense. 
Machi-san, you make a great instructor.

09:52.330 --> 09:54.990
Sorry, I got carried away.

09:55.290 --> 09:57.150
No, I'm glad.

09:57.150 --> 10:02.610
You're making the effort so we 
can enjoy a delicious meal.

10:04.120 --> 10:05.990
I'm kind of embarrassed.

10:08.050 --> 10:09.610
It should be good now.

10:09.610 --> 10:11.570
Okay, shall we eat?

10:11.570 --> 10:12.510
Yes!

10:25.270 --> 10:28.270
Kawanaka Shopping District

10:26.080 --> 10:28.280
I'm stuffed!

10:29.190 --> 10:30.420
Did you like it?

10:30.420 --> 10:31.110
Yes.

10:31.110 --> 10:32.780
Great!

10:33.550 --> 10:38.920
I didn't expect this to be the day I'd finally get to 
experience a barbecue place like I'd wanted to.

10:38.920 --> 10:40.890
It's time I cheered up.

10:41.290 --> 10:42.120
Sure.

10:47.890 --> 10:49.120
Gum.

10:49.120 --> 10:50.400
It's orange-flavored!

10:50.690 --> 10:54.110
And it looks like our
 "minister of meat" is satisfied.

10:54.110 --> 10:55.940
Thanks for coming along.

10:55.940 --> 10:59.630
Of course. Today was so much fun.

10:59.630 --> 11:00.890
That much?

11:04.560 --> 11:10.430
I realize the island isn't the only reason
 I have a skewed perspective.

11:19.700 --> 11:20.880
May I...

11:24.570 --> 11:25.840
Princess!

11:27.940 --> 11:29.470
Here you go, Princess.

11:29.470 --> 11:31.080
Thank you.

11:33.150 --> 11:36.340
Would you mind if I ate with you?

11:38.780 --> 11:42.350
We'll get yelled at if we 
get your clothes dirty.

11:42.840 --> 11:43.930
Come on, let's go.

11:43.930 --> 11:44.720
Yeah.

11:52.820 --> 11:58.950
When I think back, maybe as a 
child I was used to giving up.

12:01.340 --> 12:06.230
But now that I'm living away from the 
island by choice, here's what I think.

12:06.870 --> 12:11.230
I must keep moving forward and learning, 
not just give up because I'm incapable.

12:12.630 --> 12:14.290
You're right.

12:14.770 --> 12:20.260
Even now, I have lots of things where
 I'm liable to give up, so you dazzle me.

12:20.500 --> 12:22.000
I do?

12:22.000 --> 12:22.690
Yeah.

12:24.390 --> 12:29.930
But when I see the two of them 
smiling after that meat dinner,

12:29.930 --> 12:33.140
it makes me glad I didn't 
give up on so many things.

12:35.850 --> 12:37.580
You're right.

12:37.580 --> 12:40.400
I need to apply myself more and more, too.

12:41.790 --> 12:44.100
No, I didn't mean that!

12:44.100 --> 12:46.060
You're definitely trying hard!

12:46.060 --> 12:48.000
You don't need to overdo it.

12:48.000 --> 12:52.200
Or maybe, you're fine as you are, or...

12:53.940 --> 12:56.990
Sorry, what am I even saying?

12:56.990 --> 12:59.750
It's like, you're fine the way you are.

12:59.750 --> 13:05.800
I mean, wanting to change is a good thing, 
and it's not that I don't want you to...

13:08.520 --> 13:12.370
It made me happy to hear that
I dazzle someone, though.

13:12.370 --> 13:15.310
I'll make an effort to 
be even more dazzling.

13:17.770 --> 13:20.320
You two are so slow!

13:23.140 --> 13:25.180
Sorry, I'll hurry up!

13:31.810 --> 13:33.330
Yum!

13:33.800 --> 13:36.840
Nothing beats a popsicle after barbecue!

13:40.960 --> 13:43.010
You want one, Goshiki-san?

13:43.010 --> 13:45.340
I thought I'd have some coffee.

13:47.130 --> 13:48.460
Where's Kuga-san?

13:49.040 --> 13:52.530
In his room. He holed up 
as soon as we got home.

13:52.970 --> 13:54.140
Work?

13:54.140 --> 13:57.980
I don't know. But I was hoping we'd 
play a card game or something.

13:58.470 --> 14:00.230
I see.

14:03.510 --> 14:07.610
<i>Did I make some careless mistake earlier?</i>

14:08.500 --> 14:11.600
<i>Was it another failure to communicate?</i>

14:13.120 --> 14:14.610
It's spilling all over!

14:21.140 --> 14:23.110
I'm such a mess.

14:23.110 --> 14:26.390
There must have been something more 
I could have said to her.

14:28.190 --> 14:34.750
<i>I have plenty I want to convey, 
but when I try, the words fail me.</i>

14:40.940 --> 14:43.260
I know, a letter!

14:43.260 --> 14:45.150
Maybe I can put it into writing instead!

14:46.970 --> 14:52.650
"You've been dependable ever since I met you."

14:57.960 --> 14:59.780
I can keep going.

15:01.200 --> 15:03.010
Which do you like best?

15:05.060 --> 15:07.040
I like this one.

15:07.780 --> 15:09.430
This is love!

15:09.800 --> 15:14.670
No, maybe I've always been 
an absentminded person.

15:16.830 --> 15:20.140
Let's see, how do I word this?

15:20.560 --> 15:23.800
C-Can't think of the right words.

15:23.800 --> 15:24.700
I know!

15:26.440 --> 15:28.200
I'll use illustrations!

15:29.170 --> 15:30.270
Okay!

15:31.490 --> 15:34.870
At first, I definitely...
but once we started working,
I truly was surprised.
You could have fooled me that
you'd never been an assistant


15:32.130 --> 15:33.810
Let's see.

15:34.730 --> 15:41.070
"When I say 'beautiful,' I mean things like 
your posture and pen work, but now..."

15:41.070 --> 15:44.240
But now, um...

15:44.590 --> 15:47.590
"and pen work, but now"

15:47.850 --> 15:49.600
You know what!

15:49.970 --> 15:52.080
Drawing a manga would be faster!

16:04.090 --> 16:05.500
Done!

16:06.520 --> 16:07.810
Okay.

16:10.950 --> 16:12.050
Yes?

16:12.050 --> 16:14.050
Uh, it's Kuga.

16:14.880 --> 16:17.580
I haven't gotten dressed yet.

16:18.020 --> 16:20.520
Of course! I'm sorry.

16:20.520 --> 16:24.490
I tried drawing... writing a letter, 
if you'd like to read it.

16:24.490 --> 16:26.000
I'll leave it in your mailbox.

16:29.840 --> 16:32.180
I'm sorry about yesterday.

16:32.180 --> 16:34.850
I'm sure I said something careless to you.

16:35.220 --> 16:37.230
What are you talking about?

16:39.000 --> 16:41.720
Never mind, come on in.

16:42.190 --> 16:44.190
Th-Thanks.

16:49.230 --> 16:50.980
What's this?

16:54.290 --> 16:57.540
I thought about what I'm 
currently capable of.

16:57.540 --> 17:02.490
Maybe good communication isn't 
something I'll master anytime soon,

17:02.490 --> 17:05.750
but I can practice the art techniques 
that were pointed out to me.

17:08.580 --> 17:12.250
Also, it's a shame I haven't 
read the classics.

17:12.800 --> 17:16.740
I started reading
 <i>Magical Girl-Thing From Another World</i>,

17:16.740 --> 17:19.130
and it was so good I couldn't stop!

17:19.440 --> 17:22.490
It's hard to believe it's 
over thirty years old!

17:22.760 --> 17:25.190
<i>Goshiki-san is incredible.</i>

17:26.430 --> 17:28.380
<i>How embarrassing!</i>

17:28.380 --> 17:34.520
<i>Here she is putting her best foot forward, 
and what have </i>I<i> been drawing?!</i>

17:34.840 --> 17:37.270
<i>I-It might creep her out.</i>

17:37.570 --> 17:39.570
Oh, you had a letter.

17:39.570 --> 17:40.470
I'll read it.

17:40.470 --> 17:42.550
Oh, this is just...

17:43.440 --> 17:45.780
Can't you show it to me?

17:49.510 --> 17:51.290
It's...

17:49.630 --> 17:51.300
To Goshiki-san

17:52.000 --> 17:57.020
Well, I started writing 
about your good points,

17:57.020 --> 17:59.810
but it just wasn't coming together as words.

18:00.090 --> 18:02.220
You know what, just forget about it!

18:02.220 --> 18:03.290
Sorry.

18:14.210 --> 18:17.690
S-Sorry! I <i>really</i> should've 
minded my own business!

18:18.800 --> 18:22.740
No, it's just a surprise.

18:27.610 --> 18:32.580
<i>At first, I simply thought a 
dependable person had arrived.</i>

18:33.220 --> 18:39.110
<i>The Engagement Pact and your background 
are certainly points of concern.</i>

18:38.840 --> 18:44.060
I do have the choice not to fall in love.

18:39.720 --> 18:44.780
<i>But the way you readily accept new things,</i>

18:44.060 --> 18:46.890
I was unsure, and you told me which one you liked.

18:44.060 --> 18:46.890
I like this one.

18:44.780 --> 18:50.970
<i>and the way you have a different perspective, 
and speak your mind rather than being timid...</i>

18:46.890 --> 18:50.560
If you need help, please tell me honestly.

18:51.370 --> 18:57.900
<i>It's hard to put into words, but the way you 
see things is always refreshing for me.</i>

18:54.530 --> 18:58.490
It's hard to put into words, but the way you see things is always refreshing for me.

18:59.680 --> 19:02.310
Why is it so...

19:02.740 --> 19:09.920
This is love!

19:03.430 --> 19:09.090
<i>When you seem happy or like you're having fun, 
it makes me very happy, too.</i>

19:09.910 --> 19:15.770
<i>That one time that rainy day, 
I felt the tension just melt away.</i>

19:09.920 --> 19:15.750
Maybe I am an absentminded person.

19:18.610 --> 19:20.140
I wanted you to know.

19:21.670 --> 19:29.600
<i>I realize there are many thing I can't do, 
and yet I try to hide that behind a brave front.</i>

19:30.550 --> 19:36.520
<i>But you readily admit such things, 
and get yourself right out of a jam.</i>

19:37.720 --> 19:41.110
<i>I thought to myself, how strong and lovely.</i>

19:42.170 --> 19:46.020
You have plenty of wonderful 
traits the way you are!

19:50.610 --> 19:52.650
This is eighty pages long!

19:56.920 --> 19:58.150
I'm so happy!

20:27.020 --> 20:28.950
I'll treasure it.

20:42.340 --> 20:44.340
Yudai Sano

20:42.850 --> 20:44.340
It's Sano-kun.

20:47.220 --> 20:49.460
Long time! What's up?

20:49.460 --> 20:50.850
<i>Long time, indeed.</i>

20:51.290 --> 20:55.720
Uh... I heard you have an assistant 
named Shiori Goshiki.

20:56.070 --> 20:59.230
Oh! Did she hit <i>you</i> up for work?

20:59.620 --> 21:03.670
Well, I wasn't sure whether to mention this.

21:03.670 --> 21:08.020
But when I asked whether she'd tried 
working with you, she was like...

21:08.820 --> 21:11.750
Kuga-san sure is lovely.

21:12.190 --> 21:14.930
<i>You've got a fan </i>in love<i> with </i>you<i>, no </i>doubt<i>!</i>

21:17.860 --> 21:20.500
W-We're actually dating.

21:20.950 --> 21:21.910
Huh?!

21:22.380 --> 21:27.240
I was dwelling so much on whether I should 
tell you, I got all short with her!

21:27.630 --> 21:29.510
I'm really sorry.

21:29.910 --> 21:31.970
No, it's okay.

21:31.970 --> 21:33.800
<i>Now I get it.</i>

21:33.800 --> 21:37.410
<i>I'll have her come by again, then. 
And I don't need to worry about all this.</i>

21:37.410 --> 21:38.890
Really?

21:39.070 --> 21:42.270
She's a little unusual, but interesting.

21:42.270 --> 21:44.000
And above all, she's got skills.

21:44.000 --> 21:45.110
You're cool with it?

21:45.110 --> 21:47.800
Of course! I'll tell her, too.

21:47.800 --> 21:49.900
Awesome, please do.

21:55.990 --> 21:57.540
Good.

21:57.540 --> 22:00.160
Good for you, Goshiki-san.

23:46.040 --> 23:47.430
Got the flowers?

23:47.430 --> 23:48.310
Got 'em.

23:48.310 --> 23:50.090
Got the candle and incense sticks?

23:50.090 --> 23:50.900
Got 'em!

23:50.900 --> 23:52.830
Good, we're ready!

23:52.830 --> 23:54.930
Time to go visit the grave!

23:54.930 --> 23:56.410
Go! Go!

23:55.950 --> 23:59.900
<b><b>Episode 7</b></b>

23:55.950 --> 23:59.900
<b>A Slight Fever with the Princess</b>

23:56.410 --> 23:57.710
So much excitement!
